/**
 * @mainpage Zappy Server
 *
 * @section intro Overview
 * The Zappy server runs the authoritative simulation of the Zappy world and
 * serves two kinds of clients over TCP:
 * - **AI** clients: the players, each driving one creature through the text
 *   protocol (Forward, Look, Incantation, ...).
 * - **GUI** clients: graphical observers that receive a live stream of events
 *   describing the world.
 *
 * A single thread multiplexes all sockets with @c poll() and advances the game
 * at a fixed frequency, interleaving network I/O and simulation ticks.
 *
 * @section layers Layered architecture
 * The code is organised in concentric layers (inner layers never depend on
 * outer ones):
 * - @c domain/ — the model and rules: @ref Map, @ref GameEngine, the
 *   @ref Client hierarchy and the network interfaces (@ref ISocket, @ref IPoll,
 *   @ref INetworkProvider, @ref INetworkLoader).
 * - @c infrastructure/ — concrete adapters over the OS: @ref Socket, @ref Poll
 *   and @ref NetworkLoader, all reached through a dynamically loaded backend.
 * - @c application/ — orchestration: @ref Server (the main loop), the command
 *   and event Visitors, the client handlers.
 * - @c presentation/ — protocol entry points: command parsing, dispatch tables
 *   and the per-type client handlers.
 * - @c shared/ — cross-cutting utilities: @ref CircularBuffer, @ref ILogger,
 *   @ref ServerException.
 *
 * @section patterns Design patterns
 * The most important patterns are documented as modules:
 * - @ref visitor_ai — AI command Visitor.
 * - @ref visitor_gui — GUI command Visitor.
 * - @ref visitor_event — GUI event Visitor.
 *
 * Other patterns are described on their pivot types: Strategy on
 * @ref IClientDataHandler, Facade + Dependency Injection on @ref Server /
 * @ref INetworkProvider, Adapter on @ref NetworkLoader / @ref Socket, and
 * Template Method on @ref Client.
 *
 * @section poll I/O multiplexing
 * The cooperative single-thread model relies on the @c poll system call. See
 * @ref IPoll for a detailed walkthrough of how the watch list is maintained,
 * how @c POLLOUT is
 * armed on demand, and how the poll timeout is kept in step with the game ticks.
 *
 * @section protocol Protocol
 * The wire protocol (AI commands with their durations, GUI commands and the
 * server-to-GUI events) is documented on each command/event class and follows
 * the project's Zappy protocol specification.
 *
 * @section build Generating this documentation
 * From the repository root:
 * @verbatim
 * doxygen server/Doxyfile          # HTML -> docs/doxygen/html/index.html
 * make -C docs/doxygen/latex       # PDF  -> docs/doxygen/latex/refman.pdf
 * @endverbatim
 */
